From 30fa479a3d9c6577c0ea3428abf0497d0fa7a177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:20:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] chore(art): drop the availability table, its
 generators, and its plumbing

The unconditional rewrite made all of this dead weight: with nothing choosing a
printing, there is nothing to look up, so the measured per-printing availability
table no longer has a reader.

Removed: scripts/gen-derived-art-availability.sh and its two Python helpers, the
`__SCRYFALL_IMAGES_AVAILABILITY_URL_TEMPLATE__` define from vite.config.ts,
vitest.config.ts and vite-env.d.ts, and the generated sidecar itself.

That is the concrete benefit of the rewrite: the fork no longer maintains a
per-printing table for any locale, and a fresh build no longer spends ~6 minutes
producing one.
